    "problemStatement": "Stack has a positive integer P(P&gt;1)P(P &gt; 1)P(P&gt;1).\n\nHe starts a game where his initial score is 000.\n\nIn the ithi^{th}ith turn, with a probability of 12\\frac{1}{2}21​, Stack adds 1Pi−1\\frac{1}{P^{i-1}}Pi−11​ to his score.\n\nStack stops after NNN turns.\n\nLet SiS_iSi​ be his score after iii turns and F(i)F(i)F(i) denote the expected value of Si2S_i^2Si2​.\n\nFor each integer i(1≤i≤N)i(1 \\leq i \\leq N)i(1≤i≤N), find the value of F(i)F(i)F(i) modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\nThe only line of input contains two space-separated positive integers NNN and PPP, as mentioned in the statement.\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nPrint NNN space-separated integers. For each integer i(1≤i≤N)i(1 \\leq i \\leq N)i(1≤i≤N), output the value of F(i)F(i)F(i) modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n\nFormally, let M=998244353M=998244353M=998244353. It can be shown that the answer can be expressed as an irreducible fraction xy\\frac{x}{y}yx​, where xxx and yyy are integers and y≢0(modM)y \\not \\equiv 0 \\pmod{M}y≡0(modM).\n\nOutput the integer equal to x⋅y−1 mod Mx \\cdot y^{-1} \\bmod M x⋅y−1modM.\n\nIn other words, output such an integer zzz that 0≤z&lt;M0 \\leq z &lt; M0≤z&lt;M and z⋅y≡x(modM)z \\cdot y \\equiv x \\pmod{M}z⋅y≡x(modM).\n.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤N≤3⋅1051 \\leq N \\leq 3 \\cdot 10^51≤N≤3⋅105",
      "2≤P≤1052 \\leq P \\leq 10^52≤P≤105"
    ],
